\name{cellucid_gene_set_save}
\alias{cellucid_gene_set_save}
\title{Keep a gene set}
\usage{
cellucid_gene_set_save(viewer, name, genes, description = "")
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{name}{The set's name. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{genes}{Gene names. A vector or list of text (at least 1 character) (at least 1 item). Required.}
\item{description}{What the set is. Text. Default \code{""}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
A named list of genes, kept with the dataset for analyses and sessions; a later set of the same name replaces it.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{gene-set.save} (Genes). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labelled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{gene-sets}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_gene_set_save(viewer, genes = "x",
      name = "x")
  print(request)
